{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@property","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"text":"nonatomic","kind":"keyword"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NSExpression","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)NSExpression"},{"text":" * ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hillshadeMethod","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":";"}],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["occ"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default value of this property is an expression that evaluates to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"standard"},{"text":". Set this property to ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to reset it to the default value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can set this property to an expression containing any of the following:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Constant ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLNHillshadeMethod","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Any of the following constant string values:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": The legacy hillshade method.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"basic","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Basic hillshade. Uses a simple physics model where the reflected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"light intensity is proportional to the cosine of the angle between the incident","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"light and the surface normal. Similar to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gdaldem"},{"type":"text","text":" default algorithm."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"combined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Hillshade algorithm whose intensity scales with slope. Simi